## Core problem (unchanged in intent)

The builder knows roles and capability quantities. It should also know, per
selected spell: does a duplicate give full value; can it be reflected (whole
or in part); can its buff be purged / its debuff cleansed; what CC class it
applies; what named effects it carries — and surface that in scoring
adjustments, duplicate warnings, the dossier UI, and the composition
analysis.

## 1. Interaction data model

New curated file `pipeline/interactions.yaml` (validated, like capability
sheets), keyed by spell UniqueName, compiled by a new
`pipeline/build_interactions.py` into `out/interactions.json` (embedded in
the dataset like `item_stats`). Per spell:

- `effect_name` — the named buff/debuff it applies (identity for stacking)
- `duplicate` — the enum in §2, per component where they differ
- `components` — list of `{id, kind: damage|dot|ground_dot|buff|debuff|cc,
  reflect, cleanse, purge, duplicate, cc_type?, notes?}` (§3)
- `nonstacking_caps` — capability names whose party supply should count
  once when two members equip this same spell (ONLY on `verified` entries;
  `unknown` never changes a score)
- provenance: `confidence: verified|likely|community_reported|unknown`,
  `source`, `as_of`, `verified_patch` — chapter-2 conventions

Structural pre-pass (same evidence-first pattern as ranged_presence): the
pinned snapshot's spell descriptions state some facts outright — "the
damage cannot be reflected" (Death Curse, Inner Shadow, Flaming Phoenix's
burn, Raging Storm, Ice Crystal's explosion, Meteor, …) and charge/stack
language. `build_interactions.py` extracts those sentences as verified
structural facts (source = spell description @ snapshot commit) and the
curated file maps them onto components; anything the game does not state is
`unknown`, never guessed.

## 2. Duplicate stacking enum (unchanged)

`full | damage_only | refresh | override | shared_stack |
unique_effect_only | partial | does_not_stack | unknown` — with the
original definitions. `unknown` is always preferable to guessing, and
`unknown` must have zero scoring effect.

## 3. Component-level interactions (unchanged in intent)

An E may carry initial hit + ground DoT + anti-heal with different reflect/
stacking behavior — Dawnsong's FIREPHOENIX is the seed proof: burn DoT
verified non-reflectable by description, initial hit unstated → unknown,
healing-received reduction a separate component. Spell-level rollup:
all-same → that status; differing known statuses (or known + unknown mix)
→ `partial`; nothing known → `unknown`.

## 4. Interaction categories

As originally listed (duplicate/reflect/purge/cleanse/CC classes/offensive
utility/defensive utility/interrupts/damage profile) — mapped where
possible onto EXISTING structures: CC classes and anti-heal/pierce already
exist as parse_dumps flags + evidence-linted capabilities; the interaction
file adds what is genuinely new (reflect, purge/cleanse-ability of the
effect, duplicate semantics, named effects, interrupt facts where the
description states them). Do not duplicate the capability sheets.

## 5. Global PvP rules layer

Extend `pipeline/templates/mechanics.yaml` (it already holds Focus Fire /
Resilience + penetration placeholder, AoE Escalation + CC-escalation
placeholder, Disarray). Add placeholder entries — `null` values + wiki/TODO
citations, same style as `resilience_penetration: null` — for CC
diminishing returns and healing-modifier rules. Numbers only when sourced;
never invented.

## 6. Weapon UI (dossier)

Add a "PvP interactions" block to the weapon dossier drawer: per-spell
badges (NON-REFLECTABLE, ANTI-HEAL, PIERCE, STUN/ROOT/…, DUPLICATE:FULL /
PARTIAL / UNKNOWN…) with a confidence chip and human-readable tooltips
(§14 texts). Reuse the existing badge/drawer styling. Unknown renders as
"unknown", never hidden.

## 7. Duplicate warnings in the roster

When two members field the same weapon (or the same spell via different
weapons), show a notice in the existing advice area: severity `info`
(verified full value) / `warning` (a utility component does not stack or is
shared) / `high` (the weapon's template-active value is substantially
non-stacking) / and an honest "not stated by game data — verify before
stacking" for `unknown`. The message names the exact effect, never
"duplicate weapon bad".

## 8. Recommendation engine

Already gap-driven. The genuinely new scoring rule: when two members'
SCORED COMBOS include the same spell whose interaction entry is verified
non-stacking for given capabilities, party supply for those caps counts
that spell once (max, not sum). Implemented in BOTH engines, covered by the
parity suite; `unknown`/`likely`/`community_reported` entries never change
scores. Forge/recommend inherit automatically through comp_score.

## 9. Team-level analysis

`Engine.analyze(party, combos)` (+ JS mirror) assembling: strengths (caps
at/above target), missing capabilities (existing weakness logic),
duplicate conflicts (§7 data), cc/utility/damage-profile coverage from
capability evidence + interaction badges, and the existing recommendations.
Thin assembly over existing pieces — no parallel scoring path.

## 10. Content dependence

Inherited: interactions feed capabilities and warnings; capabilities are
already weighted per content template + style. No new weighting system now;
the interaction file's shape must simply not block per-content interaction
weights later.

