## 12. Data reliability — reuse chapter 2

Confidence/source/as_of/verified_patch on every entry; structural facts
cite the spell description at the pinned snapshot commit; the compiled
output participates in the provenance manifest and the release gate; the
patch-staleness warning machinery (evidence_lint's patch index) applies to
interaction evidence spells too where practical.

## 13. Filters

A compact advanced-filter row in the existing weapon picker: toggle chips
for has-purge / cleanse / anti-heal / pierce / hard CC / displacement /
interrupt / non-reflectable damage / duplicate-friendly. Driven by existing
capability evidence + interaction badges. Keep it modest; don't crowd the
rail.

## 14. Tooltips (unchanged)

Human-readable explanations for every enum value, as originally specified.

## 15. Architecture requirements (adapted)

- inspect before modifying; extend, never fork datasets
- spell UniqueNames as identity; weapons reference spells
- interaction data separate from presentation; scoring change in BOTH
  engines with parity proven at 1e-9
- no hardcoded compositions; unknown over invention
- all existing gates stay green: golden 24/24, forge 11/11, V4 role ≥70%,
  parity 60/60 + embed, codec 24/24, patch-history 14/14, lint clean,
  provenance 24/24, builds 44/44

## 16. Tests (`tests/test_interactions.py`)

- `damage_only` duplicate (synthetic verified fixture) → supply counts the
  utility cap once, analyzer emits `warning`
- Realmbreaker + Incubus → different named effects, NO conflict
- partial reflect: mixed component statuses → spell-level `partial`
  (Dawnsong: unknown initial + verified non-reflect DoT → `partial`)
- missing utility: comp without cleanse → analyzer missing list includes it
- no false duplicate: two different pierce spells → no conflict
- `unknown` entries change no score (fitness identical with the entry
  removed)
- twin-engine parity on a duplicate-heavy party with a non-stacking fixture

